            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "EXAMPLE 2: FROG PARTY\n\nIn this example we are using the Fallback node to get some unique behavior from the Perlin Generator node. Working at signal flow, the Fallback node only updates when the incoming value is larger than its current value. Because the Perlin Generator runs from -1 to 1 we get a lot of time where the Fallback node remains at 0. This causes the erratic/jumpy behavior of the shapes.\n"
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
